From: hal@alumni.cco.caltech.edu (Hal Finney)
Subject: Re:  Living in alien VR

David Jevans is using a common misconception about QM, that it is
basically less precise than Newtonian physics.  Actually, QM is a
very precise theory, but the things it is precise about (quantum
states) are not things we can observe easily or directly.  It's possible
to put a particle into, say, a "spin up" state with arbitrarily high
precision.  And it will stay there (if not subject to outside forces).

There are even interpretations of QM, such as the many-worlds interpretation
that we've discussed here at some length, which are perfectly deterministic
(not that determinism has much to do with saving bits).

Hal

