Date: Thu, 14 Jan 93 17:45:31 PST
From: hal@alumni.cco.caltech.edu (Hal Finney)
Subject: Re:  Missing Gray Goo explained

Re Eli's comment about matter simulations:

I think it will be very hard in VR to realistically simulate many phenomena
that are quite commonplace, but which involve large numbers of particles
in chaotic conditions: sand falling through an hourglass; water pouring
from a pitcher into a glass; the curl of smoke rising from a cigarette;
etc.  These all seem to have the property that behavior at any particular
scale depends in detail on the behavior at a smaller scale.  It's possible
that clever algorithms can be developed to mimic these behaviors without
requiring in-depth simulation, but there are no guarantees.  It may be
that the only way to enjoy a walk on the wet/dry sand of the beach, watching
the waves roll in (and completing your walk before the universe expires),
will be outside of a VR.

