I was skeptical about the true value of electronic reputations. But 
I see recent proof that there is value. Yesterday, a
sarcastic, mocking newsgroup was created: alt.fan.david-sternlight.

He is probably familiar to most on the list. David has been
one of the most prolific posters to sci.crypt,
alt.security.pgp, and others over the legality and ethics of
using PGP. No amount of rational, well crafted replies would
stop his torrent of flamage. But the new newsgroup did. He
just posted a message that he will no longer post about legal,
ethical, patents, and other issued.

It took a sledgehammer, but he finally realized that his
reuptation was nearly destroyed thru his own actions. This has
convinced this skeptic.

